Content shell: deny by default what a browser would ask about.

The shell grants geolocation, motion sensors, payment handlers, background
sync and fetch, idle detection, NFC and MIDI to every site without asking,
for Chromium's browser tests. zebkit is the shell's: every page it showed
could read the device's location (Wi-Fi networks were looked up for it)
and whether the person was at the machine. A browser asks; an engine has
no prompt, so these are now denied unless the application or an agent
grants them (CDP's Browser.setPermission overrides this). The screen wake
lock, which tells a site nothing, stays granted.

--- a/content/shell/browser/shell_permission_manager.cc
+++ b/content/shell/browser/shell_permission_manager.cc
@@ -26,29 +26,26 @@
 
 bool IsAllowlistedPermissionType(PermissionType permission) {
   switch (permission) {
+    // zebkit: only what tells nothing about the person or their machine is
+    // granted without asking. A browser would ask; an engine has no prompt,
+    // so the rest is denied unless the application or an agent grants it
+    // (CDP's Browser.setPermission, which overrides this).
+    case PermissionType::WAKE_LOCK_SCREEN:
+      return true;
+
+    // zebkit: denied by default. Location (the device's Wi-Fi networks are
+    // looked up for it), motion sensors, whether the person is idle, NFC,
+    // payment handlers, work after the page is closed, MIDI devices.
     case PermissionType::GEOLOCATION:
     case PermissionType::GEOLOCATION_APPROXIMATE:
     case PermissionType::SENSORS:
     case PermissionType::PAYMENT_HANDLER:
